uction mailbox. Mailbox\nadministration uses native `x:Account/*`, `x:Domain/*` and `x:AppPassword/*` methods."},"3831":{"id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup-34","page_id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup#what-is-stalwart","content":"Stalwart Mail Server is a modern, Rust-based mail server distributed as a single binary. It supports SMTP, IMAP, JMAP, and includes built-in spam filtering, DKIM, and a management API."},"3832":{"id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup-35","page_id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup#what-is-stalwart","content":"NorthRelay uses Stalwart in a **split-role architecture** with two separate instances:"},"3833":{"id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup-36","page_id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup#what-is-stalwart","content":"| Instance           | Role            | Location      | Purpose                                                              |\n| ------------------ | --------------- | ------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Outbound Relay** | Queue + routing | Sanctuary VPS | Accepts SMTP submissions, routes to the sending relay, manages queue |","table":"table-0"},"3834":{"id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup-37","page_id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup#what-is-stalwart","content":"| Instance            | Role        | Location    | Purpose                                                |\n| ------------------- | ----------- | ----------- | ------------------------------------------------------ |\n| **Inbound Mailbox** | IMAP + JMAP | Mailbox VPS | Receives inbound mail, user mailboxes, dashboard inbox |","table":"table-0"},"3835":{"id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup-38","page_id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup#what-is-stalwart","content":"These are independent Stalwart instances with separate configurations, separate admin tokens, and separate Management APIs."},"3836":{"id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup-39","page_id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup#outbound-relay-sanctuary","content":"The relay instance handles all outbound email:"},"3837":{"id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup-40","page_id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup#outbound-relay-sanctuary","content":"Key characteristics:"},"3838":{"id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup-41","page_id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup#outbound-relay-sanctuary","content":"Runs on the Sanctuary VPS alongside the dashboard"},"3839":{"id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup-42","page_id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup#outbound-relay-sanctuary","content":"Uses host networking in Docker for SMTP port binding"},"3840":{"id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup-43","page_id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup#outbound-relay-sanctuary","content":"Routes every email, on every tier, to the single sending relay (`sovereign.north-pipe.ca`)"},"3841":{"id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup-44","page_id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup#outbound-relay-sanctuary","content":"DKIM signing is **disabled** (handled by OpenDKIM on relay VPSes)"},"3842":{"id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup-45","page_id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup#outbound-relay-sanctuary","content":"Management API on port 8080 (internal only)"},"3843":{"id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup-46","page_id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup#inbound-mailbox","content":"The mailbox instance handles all inbound email and user inbox access:"},"3844":{"id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup-47","page_id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup#inbound-mailbox","content":"Key characteristics:"},"3845":{"id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup-48","page_id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup#inbound-mailbox","content":"Runs on a dedicated Mailbox VPS"},"3846":{"id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup-49","page_id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup#inbound-mailbox","content":"MX records point here (`mx.northrelay.ca`)"},"3847":{"id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup-50","page_id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup#inbound-mailbox","content":"Provides IMAP and JMAP access for dashboard inbox"},"3848":{"id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup-51","page_id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup#inbound-mailbox","content":"Uses SQL directory queries against PostgreSQL for authentication"},"3849":{"id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup-52","page_id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup#inbound-mailbox","content":"Each user's inbox email = their subdomain slot email"},"3850":{"id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup-53","page_id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup#toml-configuration-basics","content":"Stalwart's static configuration uses TOML format. Key sections:"},"3851":{"id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup-54","page_id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup#authentication","content":"The `fallback-admin.secret` is the token used for Management API and CLI authentication."},"3852":{"id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup-55","page_id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup#queue-and-routing","content":"See Outbound routing below for the details."},"3853":{"id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup-56","page_id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup#management-api","content":"The Management API runs on port 8080 and provides HTTP endpoints for administration."},"3854":{"id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup-57","page_id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup#authentication-1","content":"All API requests require authentication:"},"3855":{"id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup-58","page_id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup#cli-tool","content":"The Stalwart CLI (`stalwart-cli`) manages runtime configuration stored in RocksDB."},"3856":{"id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup-59","page_id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup#ip-blocking-prevention","content":"> **This is the most common operational issue with Stalwart.**"},"3857":{"id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup-60","page_id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup#ip-blocking-prevention","content":"Stalwart has an auto-ban feature that blocks IP addresses after failed authentication attempts. Blocked IPs are stored in **RocksDB** (not the TOML config), so they persist across restarts."},"3858":{"id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup-61","page_id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup#symptoms","content":"SMTP connection closes immediately without a banner"},"3859":{"id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup-62","page_id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup#symptoms","content":"Telnet to port 25 connects then disconnects instantly"},"3860":{"id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup-63","page_id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup#symptoms","content":"No error in application logs - the connection is dropped at the Stalwart level"},"3861":{"id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup-64","page_id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup#prevention","content":"Add trusted IPs to the allowlist in your TOML config:"},"3862":{"id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup-65","page_id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup#prevention","content":"Or disable auto-ban entirely for development:"},"3863":{"id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup-66","page_id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup#sql-directory-queries","content":"The mailbox Stalwart instance uses SQL queries against PostgreSQL for user authentication and mail routing. These queries are stored in RocksDB and queried at runtime."},"3864":{"id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup-67","page_id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup#query-types","content":"| Query        | Purpose                                    | Supports Catch-All |\n| ------------ | ------------------------------------------ | ------------------ |\n| `recipients` | Determine if an address should be accepted | Yes                |","table":"table-1"},"3865":{"id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup-68","page_id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup#query-types","content":"| Query  | Purpose                                | Supports Catch-All |\n| ------ | -------------------------------------- | ------------------ |\n| `name` | Resolve a user account from an address | Yes                |","table":"table-1"},"3866":{"id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup-69","page_id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup#query-types","content":"| Query    | Purpose                                     | Supports Catch-All |\n| -------- | ------------------------------------------- | ------------------ |\n| `emails` | Get all allowed sender addresses for a user | Yes                |","table":"table-1"},"3867":{"id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup-70","page_id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup#query-types","content":"| Query     | Purpose                              | Supports Catch-All |\n| --------- | ------------------------------------ | ------------------ |\n| `secrets` | Get password hash for authentication | No                 |","table":"table-1"},"3868":{"id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup-71","page_id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup#query-types","content":"| Query     | Purpose                 | Supports Catch-All |\n| --------- | ----------------------- | ------------------ |\n| `members` | Group membership lookup | No                 |","table":"table-1"},"3869":{"id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup-72","page_id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup#catch-all-support","content":"The `recipients` and `name` queries include catch-all logic: if no exact match is found, they check whether the domain has `is_inbox_hosted = true` in the `domains` table. If so, all mail to that domain routes to the domain owner."},"3870":{"id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup-73","page_id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup#principal-management","content":"Stalwart principals represent user accounts. For the mailbox instance, principals are provisioned automatically during user registration."},"3871":{"id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup-74","page_id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup#principal-fields","content":"| Field  | Description                    |\n| ------ | ------------------------------ |\n| `type` | `individual` for user accounts |","table":"table-2"},"3872":{"id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup-75","page_id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup#principal-fields","content":"| Field  | Description                        |\n| ------ | ---------------------------------- |\n| `name` | Primary identifier (usually email) |","table":"table-2"},"3873":{"id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup-76","page_id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup#principal-fields","content":"| Field    | Description                                                     |\n| -------- | --------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `emails` | Array of all email addresses this principal can send/receive as |","table":"table-2"},"3874":{"id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup-77","page_id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup#principal-fields","content":"| Field     | Description                           |\n| --------- | ------------------------------------- |\n| `secrets` | Array containing bcrypt password hash |","table":"table-2"},"3875":{"id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup-78","page_id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup#principal-fields","content":"| Field   | Description                                 |\n| ------- | ------------------------------------------- |\n| `quota` | Mailbox size limit in bytes (0 = unlimited) |","table":"table-2"},"3876":{"id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup-79","page_id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup#outbound-routing","content":"The outbound relay sends every message, on every tier, through one route to the sending relay:"},"3877":{"id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup-80","page_id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup#outbound-routing","content":"| Route   | Address                                                   | Relay VPS      |\n| ------- | --------------------------------------------------------- | -------------- |\n| `relay` | `sovereign.north-pipe.ca:25` (over WireGuard, `10.0.2.2`) | `76.13.27.101` |","table":"table-3"},"3878":{"id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup-81","page_id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup#outbound-routing","content":"Rules that matter in Stalwart v0.15:"},"3879":{"id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup-82","page_id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup#outbound-routing","content":"The route address **must be a DNS hostname**, never a raw IP — a raw IP triggers a \"record not found for MX\" error. On Sanctuary, `/etc/hosts` maps `sovereign.north-pipe.ca` to the WireGuard address `10.0.2.2` so the route stays inside the tunnel."},"3880":{"id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup-83","page_id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup#outbound-routing","content":"`queue.outbound.next-hop` is ignored; only `queue.strategy.route` selects the route."},"3881":{"id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup-84","page_id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup#outbound-routing","content":"RocksDB keys override the TOML file. After changing the route, delete any stale `queue.strategy.route` / `queue.route.*` keys and run `server reload-config`."},"3882":{"id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup-85","page_id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup#outbound-routing","content":"Never set `queue.outbound.is_local` on the relay instance — it has no mailboxes."},"3883":{"id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup-86","page_id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup#outbound-routing","content":"Tier does not affect routing. See Sending Infrastructure for what protects the relay's reputation."},"3884":{"id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup-87","page_id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup#next-steps","content":"Configuration Guide - Environment variables and service configuration"},"3885":{"id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup-88","page_id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup#next-steps","content":"Monitoring - Health checks for Stalwart and related services"},"3886":{"id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup-89","page_id":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operators/stalwart-setup#next-steps","content":"Runbooks - Troubleshooting Stalwart issues"},"3887":{"id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server","page_id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server","type":"page","content":"MCP Server","breadcrumbs":["NorthRelay Documentation","SDKs"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server"},"3888":{"id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server-0","page_id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server","content":"NorthRelay MCP Server for AI agent integration with Claude Code, Claude Desktop, Codex, Cursor, Windsurf, and other MCP-compatible clients"},"3889":{"id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server-1","page_id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server#mcp-server","content":"MCP Server"},"3890":{"id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server-2","page_id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server#wha