ers `403 SCOPE_INSUFFICIENT` naming the scope"},"4021":{"id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server-133","page_id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server#hosted-endpoint-connects-but-shows-no-tools","content":"The client presented the wrong bearer: the server answers `401`, which most\nclients report as a failed connection. Check the token the client was given\nagainst `NORTHRELAY_MCP_AUTH_TOKEN` on the host."},"4022":{"id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server-134","page_id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server#hosted-endpoint-connects-but-shows-no-tools","content":"The client was pointed at the host root instead of `/mcp`."},"4023":{"id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server-135","page_id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server#hosted-endpoint-connects-but-shows-no-tools","content":"Adding it as a claude.ai custom connector without `NORTHRELAY_MCP_PUBLIC_URL`\nset on the instance: that dialog cannot send a bearer token, so the\ninstance has to run in connector mode."},"4024":{"id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server-136","page_id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server#hosted-endpoint-connects-but-shows-no-tools","content":"The connector reports \"Couldn't register with … sign-in service\", or\nconnects but never offers to sign in: the instance's\n`/.well-known/oauth-protected-resource` is not reachable through the\nreverse proxy, or names a platform origin the client cannot reach.\n`curl -s https://mcp.example.net/.well-known/oauth-protected-resource`\nshould answer with `authorization_servers`. A proxy that forwards only\n`/mcp` and `/healthz` has to forward that path too — the instance answers\nboth the bare path and the `/mcp`-suffixed form, so with Caddy:"},"4025":{"id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server-137","page_id":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdks/mcp-server#related","content":"TypeScript SDK for programmatic Node.js integration"},"4026":{"i