thon","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdks/python#python-sdk","content":"The official NorthRelay Python SDK (`northrelay` 1.9.0) is an async client built on httpx, with Pydantic v2 models for requests and results."},"4050":{"id":"/docs/sdks/python-21","page_id":"/docs/sdks/python","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdks/python#python-sdk","content":"**Requires Python 3.9+.** Every API method is a coroutine: call it with `await` inside an async function (FastAPI, Starlette, aiohttp, or `asyncio.run`)."},"4051":{"id":"/docs/sdks/python-22","page_id":"/docs/sdks/python","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdks/python#quick-start","content":"`async with` closes the HTTP connection pool on exit; without it, call `await client.close()` when you are done."},"4052":{"id":"/docs/sdks/python-23","page_id":"/docs/sdks/python","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdks/python#configuration","content":"| Option    | Type  | Default    | Description             |\n| --------- | ----- | ---------- | ----------------------- |\n| `api_key` | `str` | *required* | Your NorthRelay API key |","table":"table-0"},"4053":{"id":"/docs/sdks/python-24","page_id":"/docs/sdks/python","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdks/python#configuration","content":"| Option     | Type  | Default                     | Description  |\n| ---------- | ----- | --------------------------- | ------------ |\n| `base_url` | `str` | `https://app.northrelay.ca` | API base URL |","table":"table-0"},"4054":{"id":"/docs/sdks/python-25","page_id":"/docs/sdks/python","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdks/python#configuration","content":"| Option    | Type    | Default | Description                |\n| --------- | ------- | ------- | -------------------------- |\n| `timeout` | `float` | `30.0`  | Request timeout in seconds |","table":"table-0"},"4055":{"id":"/docs/sdks/python-26","page_id":"/docs/sdks/python","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdks/python#configuration","content":"| Option        | Type  | Default | Description                      |\n| ------------- | ----- | ------- | -------------------------------- |\n| `max_retries` | `int` | `3`     | Max attempts for retryable reads |","table":"table-0"},"4056":{"id":"/docs/sdks/python-27","page_id":"/docs/sdks/python","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdks/python#configuration","content":"| Option        | Type    | Default | Description                    |\n| ------------- | ------- | ------- | ------------------------------ |\n| `retry_delay` | `float` | `1.0`   | Initial retry delay in seconds |","table":"table-0"},"4057":{"id":"/docs/sdks/python-28","page_id":"/docs/sdks/python","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdks/python#configuration","content":"| Option            | Type    | Default | Description              |\n| ----------------- | ------- | ------- | ------------------------ |\n| `max_retry_delay` | `float` | `10.0`  | Cap on the backoff delay |","table":"table-0"},"4058":{"id":"/docs/sdks/python-29","page_id":"/docs/sdks/python","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdks/python#mailing-lists-and-subscriptions","content":"See the Mailing Lists guide for the full integration and the Subscriptions API for request and response details. Results are Pydantic models with snake_case attributes (`result.contact_id`, `status.unsubscribed_from_all`)."},"4059":{"id":"/docs/sdks/python-30","page_id":"/docs/sdks/python","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdks/python#subscriptions","content":"| Method                                                                                                                                                                                             | Endpoint              | Returns           |\n| -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | --------------------- | ----------------- |\n| `subscriptions.subscribe(email, *, first_name, last_name, phone, list_ids, topic_ids, tags, custom_fields, metadata, double_opt_in, confirmation_template_id, redirect_url, resubscribe, consent)` | `POST /subscriptions` | `SubscribeResult` |","table":"table-1"},"4060":{"id":"/docs/sdks/python-31","page_id":"/docs/sdks/python","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdks/python#subscriptions","content":"| Method                                     | Endpoint                                 | Returns           |\n| ------------------------------------------ | ---------------------------------------- | ----------------- |\n| `subscriptions.subscribe_request(request)` | Same, with a prepared `SubscribeRequest` | `SubscribeResult` |","table":"table-1"},"4061":{"id":"/docs/sdks/python-32","page_id":"/docs/sdks/python","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdks/python#subscriptions","content":"| Method                                                                  | Endpoint                          | Returns             |\n| ----------------------------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------- | ------------------- |\n| `subscriptions.unsubscribe(email, *, scope, list_id, topic_id, reason)` | `POST /subscriptions/unsubscribe` | `UnsubscribeResult` |","table":"table-1"},"4062":{"id":"/docs/sdks/python-33","page_id":"/docs/sdks/python","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdks/python#subscriptions","content":"| Method                     | Endpoint                     | Returns              |\n| -------------------------- | ---------------------------- | -------------------- |\n| `subscriptions.get(email)` | `GET /subscriptions/{email}` | `SubscriptionStatus` |","table":"table-1"},"4063":{"id":"/docs/sdks/python-34","page_id":"/docs/sdks/python","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdks/python#subscriptions","content":"| Method                                                                                             | Endpoint                       | Returns              |\n| -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------ | -------------------- |\n| `subscriptions.update_preferences(email, *, topics, lists, unsubscribe_all, resubscribe, consent)` | `PATCH /subscriptions/{email}` | `SubscriptionStatus` |","table":"table-1"},"4064":{"id":"/docs/sdks/python-35","page_id":"/docs/sdks/python","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdks/python#subscriptions","content":"| Method                                     | Endpoint                                          | Returns                    |\n| ------------------------------------------ | ------------------------------------------------- | -------------------------- |\n| `subscriptions.resend_confirmation(email)` | `POST /subscriptions/{email}/resend-confirmation` | `ResendConfirmationResult` |","table":"table-1"},"4065":{"id":"/docs/sdks/python-36","page_id":"/docs/sdks/python","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdks/python#subscriptions","content":"`consent` takes a dict (`ip`, `user_agent` or `userAgent`, `text`) or a `Consent` model. Emails are URL-encoded in paths for you. `unsubscribe` raises `ValueError` when `scope=\"list\"` has no `list_id` or `scope=\"topic\"` has no `topic_id`; `update_preferences` raises `ValueError` when none of `topics`, `lists` or `unsubscribe_all=True` is given. Subscription writes are not retried automatically."},"4066":{"id":"/docs/sdks/python-37","page_id":"/docs/sdks/python","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdks/python#contacts","content":"`contacts.create()` does not record consent or fire webhooks; use `subscriptions.subscribe()` when a person signs up. `bulk_upsert` creates new contacts and skips existing ones; it does not update them."},"4067":{"id":"/docs/sdks/python-38","page_id":"/docs/sdks/python","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdks/python#lists-and-members","content":"| Method                                                        | Endpoint              |\n| ------------------------------------------------------------- | --------------------- |\n| `contacts.list_lists(*, page, limit, type, search, archived)` | `GET /contacts/lists` |","table":"table-2"},"4068":{"id":"/docs/sdks/python-39","page_id":"/docs/sdks/python","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdks/python#lists-and-members","content":"| Method                                                                                                         | Endpoint          |\n| -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ----------------- |\n| `contacts.get_list(id)` / `create_list(name, description, *, type, topic_id, tracking_enabled, segment_rules)` | `/contacts/lists` |","table":"table-2"},"4069":{"id":"/docs/sdks/python-40","page_id":"/docs/sdks/python","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdks/python#lists-and-members","content":"| Method                                                                                    | Endpoint                                                       |\n| ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `contacts.update_list(id, name, description, *, topic_id, tracking_enabled, is_archived)` | `PATCH /contacts/lists/{id}` (`topic_id=None` removes the tag) |","table":"table-2"},"4070":{"id":"/docs/sdks/python-41","page_id":"/docs/sdks/python","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdks/python#lists-and-members","content":"| Method                     | Endpoint                                 |\n| -------------------------- | ---------------------------------------- |\n| `contacts.delete_list(id)` | `DELETE /contacts/lists/{id}` (archives) |","table":"table-2"},"4071":{"id":"/docs/sdks/python-42","page_id":"/docs/sdks/python","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdks/python#lists-and-members","content":"| Method                                                                         | Endpoint                           |\n| ------------------------------------------------------------------------------ | ---------------------------------- |\n| `contacts.list_members(id, *, page, limit, filter)` (alias `get_list_members`) | `GET /contacts/lists/{id}/members` |","table":"table-2"},"4072":{"id":"/docs/sdks/python-43","page_id":"/docs/sdks/python","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdks/python#lists-and-members","content":"| Method                                                                  | Endpoint                            |\n| ----------------------------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------- |\n| `contacts.add_to_list(id, contact_ids=None, *, emails, create_missing)` | `POST /contacts/lists/{id}/members` |","table":"table-2"},"4073":{"id":"/docs/sdks/python-44","page_id":"/docs/sdks/python","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdks/python#lists-and-members","content":"| Method                                                       | Endpoint                              |\n| ------------------------------------------------------------ | ------------------------------------- |\n| `contacts.remove_from_list(id, contact_ids=None, *, emails)` | `DELETE /contacts/lists/{id}/members` |","table":"table-2"},"4074":{"id":"/docs/sdks/python-45","page_id":"/docs/sdks/python","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdks/python#lists-and-members","content":"`remove_from_list` is the list owner removing someone (the membership is deleted). To record that a recipient asked to leave, use `subscriptions.unsubscribe(email, scope=\"list\", list_id=...)`."},"4075":{"id":"/docs/sdks/python-46","page_id":"/docs/sdks/python","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdks/python#csv-import","content":"When `mappings` is omitted, columns named like email, first name, last name and phone are mapped automatically. `file_name` sets the upload name when you pass bytes."},"4076":{"id":"/docs/sdks/python-47","page_id":"/docs/sdks/python","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdks/python#topics-suppression-groups","content":"`client.topics` is an alias of `client.suppression_groups`. A topic member is an address that **opted out** of that topic. Topic methods return the API response as a dict."},"4077":{"id":"/docs/sdks/python-48","page_id":"/docs/sdks/python","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdks/python#topics-suppression-groups","content":"The member methods only edit the opt-out rows. For a recipient's own choice, prefer `subscriptions.unsubscribe(..., scope=\"topic\")` or `update_preferences`, which also update tagged lists and fire webhooks."},"4078":{"id":"/docs/sdks/python-49","page_id":"/docs/sdks/python","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdks/python#signup-forms","content":"Form methods return the `data` object of the API response as a dict."},"4079":{"id":"/docs/sdks/python-50","page_id":"/docs/sdks/python","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdks/python#signup-forms","content":"`forms.submit(form_id, values)` posts answers keyed by `fieldKey` to a published form. From your own backend, `subscriptions.subscribe()` is usually the better choice."},"4080":{"id":"/docs/sdks/python-51","page_id":"/docs/sdks/python","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdks/python#webhooks","content":"`WEBHOOK_EVENT_TYPES` lists every event name the API accepts."},"4081":{"id":"/docs/sdks/python-52","page_id":"/docs/sdks/python","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdks/python#suppressions","content":"Emails are URL-encoded in paths for you. `reason` is one of `Bounce`, `Complaint`, `Unsubscribe` or `Manual`. To record a recipient's own opt-out, prefer `subscriptions.unsubscribe()`."},"4082":{"id":"/docs/sdks/python-53","page_id":"/docs/sdks/python","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdks/python#templates-and-brands-studio","content":"Every template is a Studio design. Dashboard templates use the application key `\"account\"`; a product with an `nr_app_` credential uses its own key."},"4083":{"id":"/docs/sdks/python-54","page_id":"/docs/sdks/python","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdks/python#templates-and-brands-studio","content":"`templates` and `brand_theme` are deprecated (sunset 30 April 2027). Template ids are design ids, so sending with `template_id` keeps working."},"4084":{"id":"/docs/sdks/python-55","page_id":"/docs/sdks/python","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdks/python#other-resources","content":"| Attribute | Methods                                                       |\n| --------- | ------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `emails`  | `send`, `send_template`, `schedule`, `send_batch`, `validate` |","table":"table-3"},"4085":{"id":"/docs/sdks/python-56","page_id":"/docs/sdks/python","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdks/python#other-resources","content":"| Attribute | Methods                                                                                                                   |\n| --------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `designs` | Templates, releases, previews, sends, usage, deliveries, gallery, brands, tracking domains, assets, manifests (see above) |","table":"table-3"},"4086":{"id":"/docs/sdks/python-57","page_id":"/docs/sdks/python","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdks/python#other-resources","content":"| Attribute     | Methods                 |\n| ------------- | ----------------------- |\n| `credentials` | Application credentials |","table":"table-3"},"4087":{"id":"/docs/sdks/python-58","page_id":"/docs/sdks/python","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdks/python#other-resources","content":"| Attribute   | Methods                                                |\n| ----------- | ------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `templates` | Deprecated: legacy template API (sunset 30 April 2027) |","table":"table-3"},"4088