cks divided by opens (not by sends)."],[3869,"The `recipients` and `name` queries include catch-all logic: if no exact match is found, they check whether the domain has `is_inbox_hosted = true` in the `domains` table. If so, all mail to that domain routes to the domain owner."],[1873,"The `variables` array is automatically extracted from `{{variable}}` placeholders in the subject, html, and text fields."],[4008,"The agent calls `add_list_members` with `emails` and `createMissing`; unsubscribed or suppressed addresses come back in `blocked`."],[3998,"The agent calls `check_dns` and `check_blocklist`."],[4004,"The agent calls `get_subscription_status`, which returns his lists, topics, consent evidence and any suppression."],[4010,"The agent calls `list_list_members` with `filter: \"suppressed\"`; each member carries its `suppressionStatuses`."],[4002,"The agent calls `subscribe_contact` with `doubleOptIn` and the consent text. Jane stays pending until she clicks the confirmation link."],[4006,"The agent calls `unsubscribe_contact` with `scope: \"topic\"`. Someone who unsubscribed is never re-added unless you explicitly confirm fresh consent (`resubscribe`)."],[3990,"The AI agent will call `send_email` with the appropriate parameters."],[26,"The Analytics API provides access to delivery metrics, engagement data, geographic breakdowns, and provider-level statistics. Use these endpoints to monitor your sending performance and optimize your email strategy."],[440,"The API is versioned via the URL path (`/api/v1/`). Breaking changes will be introduced under a new version prefix (e.g., `/api/v2/`). Non-breaking additions (new fields, new endpoints) are added to the current version without a version bump."],[2877,"The API key must be active — check **Dashboard → API Keys** to confirm it has not been revoked"],[2093,"The API returns a `QuotaExceededError` with a clear message"],[2352,"The Blocklist Monitor checks your domain and sending IPs against 13 industry-standard DNS-based Real-time Blocklists (RBLs). Being listed on a blocklist can severely impact your deliverability."],[3049,"The building blocks"],[119,"the busiest routes and the most recent calls, each with its status and origin;"],[3085,"The call is idempotent: calling it again for someone already on the list returns `200` and adds nothing."],[4021,"The client presented the wrong bearer: the server answers `401`, which most\nclients report as a failed connection. Check the token the client was given\nagainst `NORTHRELAY_MCP_AUTH_TOKEN` on the host."],[4022,"The client was pointed at the host root instead of `/mcp`."],[3938,"The Codex CLI, IDE extension and desktop app share `~/.codex/config.toml`\n(or a project's `.codex/config.toml`)."],[3265,"The connection is TLS-encrypted from the start. Use this if your application does not support STARTTLS, or if port 587 is blocked on your network."],[3264,"The connection starts unencrypted, then upgrades to TLS via the STARTTLS command. This is the industry standard for SMTP submission."],[2393,"The Connectivity Doctor tests the full SMTP delivery chain from NorthRelay to a destination mail server. Use it to diagnose why emails to a specific domain are failing."],[4024,"The connector reports \"Couldn't register with … sign-in service\", or\nconnects but never offers to sign in: the instance's\n`/.well-known/oauth-protected-resource` is not reachable through the\nreverse proxy, or names a platform origin the client cannot reach.\n`curl -s https://mcp.example.net/.well-known/oauth-protected-resource`\nshould answer with `authorization_servers`. A proxy that forwards only\n`/mcp` and `/healthz` has to forward that path too — the instance answers\nboth the bare path and the `/mcp`-suffixed form, so with Caddy:"],[3092,"The contact is created as `PENDING` and added to the lists. Campaigns skip it while it is `PENDING`."],[3987,"The contact, subscription, topic and form tools return structured content and carry MCP annotations (read-only, de